# Everything is stored and checked out with LF.
#
# This is not a style preference. The build and test scripts run under bash — in WSL on
# Windows, because Smart App Control blocks the interpreter natively — and a script with
# CRLF line endings fails there with "bash: \r: command not found". The .expected test
# fixtures are compared byte-for-byte too, though the runner strips \r defensively.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.svg text eol=lf
